```
The stone relief panel at the entrance base depicts:
  竹 (bamboo) — integrity, uprightness, endurance
  梅 (plum blossom) — moral perseverance in adversity
  Other auspicious plant motifs

In Chinese cultural-moral iconography:
  竹梅 (bamboo and plum) together = the 君子 (junzi /
  noble person) virtues — moral rectitude that endures
  hardship without compromising integrity.

This is ICONOGRAPHIC INSCRIPTION of the moral programme
at the architectural threshold: before entering the
hall, the visitor encounters a carved statement of
the virtue tradition the institution embodies. The
stone relief functions as an RFIG inscriptional element
encoding moral values through botanical symbolism
rather than deity imagery.
