**Architectural character:**

The exterior is a modern, purpose-built hall — cleaner, more formal, and architecturally more restrained than the elaborate folk temples in the corpus. The aesthetic is deliberately institutional: this is a virtue-teaching association, not primarily a devotional temple. The lanterns and flowers at the entrance add warmth without the dense ornamental programme of Hokkien-Teochew-style temples.

