### New grammar contribution: the word/image substitution

This analysis generates a significant extension to RFIG's existing grammar. The *substitutes* relation has been used previously for:

```
Previous uses:
  Guan Gong substitutes Sangharama (folk/Buddhist)
  Guanyin substitutes Wusheng Laomu (Xiantiandao)
  阴财神 substitutes 阳财神 (yin/yang register)

New use:
  SPIRIT_WRITING_TEXT substitutes DEITY_FIGURE
  -- at institutions where figural representation
     is doctrinally unavailable for some traditions,
     textual presence substitutes for figural presence

New ICON parameter value:
  MEDIUM: textual / calligraphic
  -- in addition to existing sculptural / painted / carved
     media, RFIG must accommodate textual objects as
     iconographic elements in their own right

